    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Vitamin deficiency disorders (e.g., Vitamin A - Night Blindness, Vitamin C - Scurvy, Vitamin D - Rickets, Vitamin B1 - Beriberi) are high-yield exam topics.",
        "Distinguish between Kwashiorkor (protein deficiency characterized by edema) and Marasmus (overall severe calorie and protein deficiency causing muscle wasting).",
        "Mineral roles: Iron deficiency leads to Anemia, Iodine deficiency leads to Goitre, and Calcium/Phosphorus are critical for bone density."
      ],
